    "content": "<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/MGT103/flm1/d16/001.webp\" alt=\"MGT103 · Ethics of Artificial Intelligence Coursera course introduction · slide 1: Ethics of Artificial Intelligence\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"960\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Ethics of Artificial Intelligence Coursera course introduction · slide 1/5</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Ethics of Artificial Intelligence<br>Taught by:<br>Viola Schiaffonati, Assoiate Professor<br>DEIB - Dept. of Electronics, Information and Bioengineering<br>Politecnico di Milano</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/MGT103/flm1/d16/002.webp\" alt=\"MGT103 · Ethics of Artificial Intelligence Coursera course introduction · slide 2: Course Introduction\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"960\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Ethics of Artificial Intelligence Coursera course introduction · slide 2/5</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Course Introduction<br>Link to the course on Coursera: https://www.coursera.org/learn/ethics-of-artificial-intelligence<br>Students are required to study all course materials and complete the course certificates provided by Coursera by Week 7 of the semester.<br>Upon submission of Coursera certificates, students will receive 5 points of Individual assignment. (The entire Individual assignment accounts for 10% of Introduction to Management course’s final grade.)</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/MGT103/flm1/d16/003.webp\" alt=\"MGT103 · Ethics of Artificial Intelligence Coursera course introduction · slide 3: Course Introduction (Cont.)\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"960\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Ethics of Artificial Intelligence Coursera course introduction · slide 3/5</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Course Introduction (Cont.)<br>This course deals with the problems created, aggravated or transformed by AI. It is intended to give students a chance to reflect on the ethical, social, and cultural impact of AI by focusing on the issues faced by and brought about by professionals in AI but also by citizens, institutions and societies. The course addresses these topics by means of case studies and examples analyzed in the light of the main ethical frameworks.</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/MGT103/flm1/d16/004.webp\" alt=\"MGT103 · Ethics of Artificial Intelligence Coursera course introduction · slide 4: Learning Objectives\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"960\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Ethics of Artificial Intelligence Coursera course introduction · slide 4/5</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Learning Objectives<br>After studying this course, you should be able to:<br>Describe the reasons for an ethical analysis applied to AI and recognize how the notion of responsibility is challenged when designing and using AI tools.<br>Identify the ethical and social impacts and implications of AI, and recognize and analyze ethical and social issues inherent in AI by means of examples and case-studies analyzed with the use of the main ethical frameworks.<br>Analyze problems through an ethical lens and use critical skills in clarifying and ethically analyzing AI in different domains of life.<br>Critically analyze the current policies for AI and use ethical and socially responsible principles in your professional life.</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/MGT103/flm1/d16/005.webp\" alt=\"MGT103 · Ethics of Artificial Intelligence Coursera course introduction · slide 5: Course Structure\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"960\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Ethics of Artificial Intelligence Coursera course introduction · slide 5/5</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Course Structure<br>Module 1: Ethics, AI and responsibility<br>2 videos, 2 readings<br>1 graded quiz<br>Module 2: Case – studies, examples and ethical frameworks<br>5 videos, 5 readings<br>1 graded quiz<br>Module 3: Issues and challenges<br>5 videos, 5 readings<br>1 graded quiz<br>Module 4: Governance and policies<br>2 videos, 2 readings<br>1 graded quiz</p></div>"
